totals={'targets':sum(r['targets']for r in repo_rows),**{v:sum(r[v]for r in repo_rows)for v in variants}};json.dump({'baselineId':baseline['id'],'repositories':len(summaries),'libraryCases':len(rows),'positiveSupportedCases':sum(bool(r['targets'])for r in rows),'modelCalls':0,'totals':totals,'repos':repo_rows},open(OUT/'aggregate.json','w'),indent=2)
lines=['# Multi-bundler static relationship experiment v1','','All eight non-esbuild subjects from the bundling dataset were evaluated. The frozen esbuild experiment is unchanged. Models invoked: **0**. These are oracle-assisted supported-pair connectivity rates, not measured model recovery or whole-library recall.','',f"Population: {len(rows)} repo/library cases ({sum(bool(r['targets'])for r in rows)} with supported targets), {totals['targets']:,} supported pairs. Exact target and initial anchor hashes match the frozen baseline for every subject. All baseline recovered-pair sets reproduce exactly; no per-library regressions.",'','| Repository | Bundler | Targets | Frozen baseline | Source-only | Improved per chunk | Cross-chunk (separate) |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in repo_rows:lines.append('| '+r['repo']+' | '+r['bundler']+' | '+str(r['targets'])+' | '+' | '.join(f"{r[v]:,} ({rate(r[v],r['targets'])})"for v in variants)+' |')
lines.append('| **Total** | | '+f"{totals['targets']:,}"+' | '+' | '.join(f"{totals[v]:,} ({rate(totals[v],totals['targets'])})"for v in variants)+' |')
versions=[]
for d in summaries:
 a=json.load(open(BASE/'results/real-app/bundling-dataset'/d['repo'].replace('/','--')/'artifacts.json'));version='Parcel '+a['build']['parcel'] if d['bundler']=='parcel'else a['subject'].get('versionEvidence','unknown');versions.append('| '+d['repo']+' | '+version+' | `'+d['commit']+'` |')
lines+=['','## Tested build evidence','','| Repository | Build version evidence | Commit |','|---|---|---|',*versions,'','Focalboard is the separate `experiments/webext` Parcel build, not its webpack application. Motrix and ZyPlayer use browser/renderer artifacts; main/preload code is excluded. Vite versions identify the selected Rolldown-backed builds, not an independently verified backend release number.','','## Interpretation','','Denominators count supported source/bundle function pairs per prepared chunk; the same source function can recur in multiple chunks. They are not counts of unique library source functions. The source-only ablation adds the shared resolver on the source side while keeping the original bundle graph. The per-chunk result additionally permits extracted bundle edges within each chunk. Cross-chunk uses the same targets and seeds but additionally permits statically resolved relationships across supplied chunks. It does not copy anchors by source identity.','',f"Per-chunk recovery gains {totals['improved-per-chunk']-totals['baseline-control']:,} supported pairs over baseline. Cross-chunk adds another {totals['improved-cross-chunk']-totals['improved-per-chunk']:,}. The final cross-chunk gains are 348 pairs in vue-admin-better, 127 in Motrix and 75 in ZyPlayer; the other subjects gain none beyond their per-chunk results. Do not pool cross-chunk gains into a per-chunk claim.",'','The radar app remains 3/12. Its frozen source inventory has 45 parse failures among 51 files, mostly TS/TSX. The graph experiment does not repair source parsing or rebuild its oracle. Small denominators and absent initial anchors limit inference there.','',"The witness audit rejected an early over-approximation: a conditional Object.keys polyfill in dashjs had created broad icon-library bridges. The final analyzer retains native-builtin alternatives and abstains on those mixed calls. The regression test and saved rejected-bridge audit document the correction. Final figures in these tables exclude the rejected edges; this audit is not an edge precision evaluation.",'','The largest remaining gap is ZyPlayer `tdesign-icons-vue-next`: 1,530/41,489 pairs recover in both improved variants, with four frozen seeds. All 39,959 remaining pairs have no accepted bundle neighbor at the fixed point. This accounts for most of the residual misses and identifies disconnected bundle-side neighborhoods as the next target for analysis; the present experiment does not prove which missing semantic relation would connect each island.','','## Per-library comparison','','Zero-supported cases remain N/A, rather than being called 0% recovery.','', '| Repository / library | Targets | Baseline | Per chunk | Cross-chunk |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in rows:lines.append('| '+r['repo']+' / `'+r['library']+'` | '+str(r['targets'])+' | '+' | '.join(f"{r[v]} ({rate(r[v],r['targets'])})"for v in ['baseline-control','improved-per-chunk','improved-cross-chunk'])+' |')
lines+=['','## Measured scale and coverage','','Times cover parsing, constraint compilation and solving for a side, excluding evaluation. RSS is the process resident memory at extraction completion, **not** a sampled peak; parser peaks may be higher. Files are parsed one at a time; the build-wide compact constraint/value state is retained. No linear-complexity claim is made.','','| Repository | Source / bundle seconds | Source / bundle RSS MiB at completion | Source / bundle AST nodes | Runtime factories | Added cross-chunk edges |','|---|---:|---:|---|---:|']
for r,d in zip(repo_rows,summaries):
 m=d['analysis']['bundle']['stats']['modules'];runtime=', '.join(f'{k}: {v}'for k,v in m.items()if v)or'flattened / helpers';lines.append(f"| {r['repo']} | {r['source_extraction_ms']/1000:.2f} / {r['bundle_extraction_ms']/1000:.2f} | {r['source_rss_mib']} / {r['bundle_rss_mib']} | {r['source_ast_nodes']:,} / {r['bundle_ast_nodes']:,} | {runtime} | {r['cross_chunk_edges']:,} |")
lines+=['','Runtime factory counts refer to explicit registered module IDs; Rolldown lazy CommonJS helper counts appear separately in each summary, not as numbered modules. Source parse failures were skipped exactly as frozen. Code-only extraction had no additional parse failures. Overflow slots and unresolved/ambiguous modeled-call counts are recorded per subject; unresolved calls are not assumed absent.','', '## Method and boundaries','','- Same source inventory, prepared target-containing chunks, oracle, supported pairs and POG seed pairs as baseline. Other saved or emitted chunks, including some runtime-helper-only chunks, were not added. Native ESM references to absent files remain unresolved.','- Both sides receive lexical/import/export/object/class/runtime relationship analysis; module registration does not imply a function-membership clique. No source/bundle initialization-function matching was introduced.','- Graph neighborhoods are undirected, radius one, with original sibling window two and 18,000-character promotion limit. Class, binding-reference and callback-reference additions are included and should not be described solely as call edges.','- Ambiguous same-chunk source identities remain in the denominator but cannot promote or bridge. Across chunks identities may recur; no identity-only transfer occurs.','- Each promotion records a checked parent witness on both graphs. Layered propagation agrees with independent queue BFS. The frontier simulator also matches original synchronous rounds on 100 deterministic random graph pairs in tests.','- This is a partial static analysis with heuristic helper recognition, singleton modeled callable targets, and bounded value sets. It is not a sound JavaScript call graph. Unknown argument/return flow, dynamic properties, async semantics, arbitrary helper rewrites and missing package entries remain unresolved. A connectivity gain does not establish edge precision or model accuracy.','', '## Mechanisms and primary references','','Rspack uses runtime module IDs and loader operations; the adapter normalizes its factory table and resolves require/export slots through scope-bound parameter roles. [Runtime API](https://www.rspack.org/api/runtime-api/module-methods).','','Rolldown combines flattened bindings, ESM chunk imports, memoized initializers and lazy CommonJS factories. The adapter models factory export objects and uses structural helper summaries; it does not depend on helper variable spelling. [Runtime implementation](https://github.com/rolldown/rolldown/blob/main/crates/rolldown/src/runtime/runtime-base.js).','','Turbopack groups module IDs and factories in registration arrays. Its context API separates require, namespace import and export publication. Getter and direct-value binding forms, optional setters, merged IDs and explicit export module IDs are modeled. [Next 16.2.6 runtime](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/v16.2.6/turbopack/crates/turbopack-ecmascript-runtime/js/src/shared/runtime/runtime-utils.ts). Next 15.5.4 emitted getter forms were checked in the frozen corpus; support is bounded by tested shapes.','','Parcel scope-hoists eligible code and retains registered wrappers for other modules. The adapter connects the lexical loader to factory module/exports objects and getter helpers. [Scope hoisting](https://parceljs.org/features/scope-hoisting/), [runtime helper implementation](https://github.com/parcel-bundler/parcel/blob/v2/packages/packagers/js/src/helpers.js).','','## Artifacts and reproduction','','- `per-library.csv`: every library, denominators, all four variant counts/rates, parse failures and gains.','- `per-repo.csv`, `aggregate.json`: recomputable aggregate and scale records.','- `<repo>/source-relations.json`, `bundle-relations.json`: code-only edges, module records, counters and exact analyzer/input hashes.','- `<repo>/target-traces.json`: evaluation-only promotion rounds, gates and paired parent witnesses.','- `validation/tests.txt`: 19 passing tests, including protocol equivalence over 100 deterministic graph pairs.','- `code/`: exact implementation used; see its README for generic manifest use and experimental commands.','','The frozen baseline verifier passed all 14,490 checksummed files after this run. The source and bundle extractor hashes in every completed result match the implementation. No existing baseline or esbuild result was overwritten.','']
